<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! face.carry.restands ~ after a root rotation the earlier items stand again once carried

After a root rotation the earlier items read in history alone until the operator's hand carries them: `kahua carry <cid>…` names the revision cids that keep standing, or `--all` names every earlier head the history reads (never both). One root-signed act at the current epoch stands them again. It runs on a person's hand alone, and no tool carries it. Every answer prints as JSON.

Under a pūlama the root signs at the pūlama's hand door, since the vessel there holds no face root: `--terms` runs every gate and prints ONE stdout line (the one unsigned act its root signs) and opens no route; the pūlama's `sign '<terms>'` checks it and signs; `--land '<answer>'` lands the signed record, where the door builds the act afresh and lands it only over a byte-equal body. Neither asks the passphrase on the vessel, and the host shim walks the pattern (`tools/lares-container.sh kahua lift|withdraw|carry`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ one-revision · every-earlier-head

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`one-revision` params=`cid/<cid> face/1 ~ carry one earlier head across the rotation`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`every-earlier-head` params=`all face/1 ~ carry every earlier head the history reads`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ cid · all · face · terms · land

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`cid` params=`takes/cid seat/1 as/<cid> ~ a revision cid that keeps standing; name several in a row, or all=true`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`all` params=`kind/switch ~ carry every earlier head the history reads, in place of naming cids`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`face` params=`takes/handle-index ~ which face's stage this call reads or writes, by persona index (a whole number from 0); absent, the one face standing open or the worn face`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`terms` params=`kind/switch ~ print the one terms line a pūlama signs; opens no route; name it or land=, never both`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`land` params=`takes/answer ~ land the signed record from a pūlama's sign answer`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ hand

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`hand` params=`who/hand key/face-root ~ one act at the current epoch, signed under the face's root out of sealed custody; a person runs it, and an AI seat names the command`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ carry-cids-or-all · kahua-hand-malformed · face-malformed

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`carry-cids-or-all` params=`cure/[[face.carry.restands all]] ~ the door says 'carry: name the revision cids that keep standing, or --all (never both)'`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`kahua-hand-malformed` params=`~ the pūlama's answer names the wrong kind, the wrong face, or both --terms and --land stood on one line`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`face-malformed` params=`~ --face names a persona index, a whole number from 0`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ carried · refused

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`carried` params=`exit/0 ~ the earlier items stand again at the current epoch; the door's answer prints as JSON`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`refused` params=`exit/1 ~ the door refused by name; the line carries its reason`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

